<title>THAILAND: China buys 15,000 tonnes of Thai raw sugar.</title>
<headline>China buys 15,000 tonnes of Thai raw sugar.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>China bought 15,000 tonnes of Thai raw sugar for prompt shipment, trade sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Misubisihi supplied 10,000 tonnes while Cargill supplied the rest, they told Reuters.  </p>
<p>Vessel Fuda, chartered by Cargill, was now loading the cargo at a Thai port while the other ship--Solar Glory--arrived on Thursday.</p>
<p>The consignments will be used for tolling, traders said. China recently issued up to 500,000 tonnes of tolling licences.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
